CAE deployment failed with `ManagedEnvironmentInvalidNetworkConfiguration` because the delegated subnet couldn't be shared with private endpoints. Previous attempts split into two subnets, but the user wants a single subnet (`snet-rebc`, `10.0.0.0/27`) with no delegation.

### Changes

- **`containerAppsEnvironment.bicep`** — Remove `vnetConfiguration` and `infrastructureSubnetId`. CAE deploys without VNet integration; private connectivity via PE on the shared subnet
- **`variable.json`** — Replace `subnetNameCae`/`subnetNamePe`/address prefixes with single `subnetName: "snet-rebc"`
- **`main.bicep` / `main-resources.bicep`** — Single existing subnet reference; all three PEs (ACR, CAE, SQL) share it
- **`module/subnet.bicep`** — Deleted. Subnet is pre-existing, not IaC-managed
- **`README.md`** — Stripped to essentials

```bicep
// Before: VNet integration required dedicated delegated subnet
resource containerAppsEnvironment ... {
  properties: {
    vnetConfiguration: {
      internal: true
      infrastructureSubnetId: infrastructureSubnetId  // conflicts with PEs
    }
  }
}

// After: no VNet integration, private access via PE on shared subnet
resource containerAppsEnvironment ... {
  properties: {
    appLogsConfiguration: { ... }
    zoneRedundant: false
  }
}
```

### Prerequisite
Subnet `snet-rebc` must exist in `vnet-internal` (`rg-net`) with CIDR `10.0.0.0/27`. No delegation required.

