Prevents users from seeing partially loaded or broken UI when network is slow or resources are still loading.

## Changes

- **index.html**: Added loading overlay with spinner shown immediately on page load (before React/JS execution)
- **src/index.css**: Loading screen styles with gradient background, spinning animation, and fade transitions
- **src/main.jsx**: Hide logic that waits for both React mount and `window.load` event to ensure all resources are ready

## Implementation

The loader displays synchronously from HTML, then JS removes it after resources load:

```javascript
// Constants match CSS transition timing
const LOADER_TRANSITION_DURATION = 500;
const MIN_LOADER_DISPLAY_TIME = 300;

// Hide after React mounts AND all resources load
if (document.readyState === "complete") {
  setTimeout(hideLoader, 100);
} else {
  window.addEventListener("load", () => {
    setTimeout(hideLoader, 100);
  });
}
```

Minimum display time prevents flickering on fast connections. Loader removes itself from DOM after fade completes.

