### Description
Adds the parent value to `filterField` function.
This is the value of the object containing the field that we are showing in the UI.
For example; if we got a translation array , we are rendering members which are part of an object.

```ts
const parentValue = {
    value:  "english title"
    _key: "en"
   _type: "internationalizedArrayStringValue"
}
```

Previously we have recommended to use the path of the member to decide to filter the field or not, because the language was store in the `_key`. Like recommended in the README;
```ts
        if (
          enclosingType.jsonType === "object" &&
          enclosingType.name.startsWith("internationalizedArray") &&
          "kind" in member
        ) {
          // Get last two segments of the field's path
          const pathEnd = member.field.path.slice(-2);
          // If the second-last segment is a _key, and the last segment is `value`,
          // It's an internationalized array value
          // And the array _key is the language of the field
          const language =
            pathEnd[1] === "value" && isKeySegment(pathEnd[0]) ? pathEnd[0]._key : null;

          return language ? selectedLanguageIds.includes(language) : false;
        }
```

Now with the changes we are adding in which the language will be stored in a `language` field we need to have access to the value, because we need to check `parentValue.language` 


```ts
        if (
          enclosingType.jsonType === "object" &&
          enclosingType.name.startsWith("internationalizedArray") &&
          "kind" in member
        ) {
          const language = parentValue.language
          return language ? selectedLanguageIds.includes(language) : false;
        }
```

